{"questions":[{"question_id":"xHdlQU9vRCF2N2Dt","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2006","year":2006,"examDate":2006,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"d-and-f-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"inner-transition-elements-lanthanoids-and-actinoids","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"lanthanoid-contraction-is-caused-due-to-2006-marks-4-xhdlqu9vrcf2n2dt.htm","content":"Lanthanoid contraction is caused due to :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"the appreciable shielding on outer electrons by 4f electrons from the nuclear charge "},{"identifier":"B","content":"the appreciable shielding on outer electrons by 5d electrons from the nuclear charge "},{"identifier":"C","content":"the same effective nuclear charge from Ce to Lu "},{"identifier":"D","content":"the imperfect shielding on outer electrons by 4f electrons from the nuclear charge "}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"The main reason of lanthanide contraction is, poor shielding of 4f electrons on the outer most shell electrons. As f orbital is defused nature so shielding of 4f electron is imperfect that is why nucleus can attract outer most shell electron easily and the size of atom decreases.\n<br><br>In lanthanides, there is poorer shielding of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.314ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 1023 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> electrons by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0